    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2jbacjztk27",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The discussion of AI in gaming is pernicious now. The idea that games are going to be the only field where humans write code unassisted is obviously wrong. But the push for that from press & fans means missing a chance to guide AI usage toward approaches that empower workers & help gaming thrive.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2jbacjztk27",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T14:34:59.037Z",
      "likes": 93,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 15,
      "score": 7.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2htyp4bhc2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "A lot of folks don't realize how much of our computer infrastructure is an improvised system prone to cascading failures. You didn't need offensive AI cyberattacks to have big outages like Microsoft/FAA. Of course, now we DO have to deal with offensive AI (but also defensive AIs and patching)",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2htyp4bhc2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T01:05:25.401Z",
      "likes": 75,
      "replies": 7,
      "reposts": 4,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 15.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2jbhzsmxk27",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "AI is a general purpose technology has good and bad impacts, the general model should be improving the good and building on it (less crunch, more innovative games, democratizing creation), while mitigating the bad (shovelware, replacing artists etc). Seeing AI as all one thing is a barrier.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2jbhzsmxk27",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T14:39:18.318Z",
      "likes": 41,
      "replies": 4,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 6.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2hsler3as2c",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "What an amazing coincidence given the IPO is days away gizmodo.com/anthropic-sa... \nOur progress is accelerating so fast that we need to be extra careful",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2hsler3as2c",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-17T00:40:04.599Z",
      "likes": 19,
      "replies": 2,
